@ckeshava I don't think this should be "fixed" by failing the transaction — the current outcome is correct; it's the intent that reads unclearly.
AMMClawback is a compliance recovery that deliberately works without holder cooperation: it already withdraws with IgnoreFreeze/IgnoreAuth and recreates deleted MPTokens. Gating the paired-asset return on the holder's reserve reintroduces the holder veto the design intentionally strips out — a holder could block clawback indefinitely by deleting the paired trustline and keeping spendable XRP below one incremental reserve. tecINSUFFICIENT_RESERVE here is a regression, not

